## `spec` fields

These are the top-level fields of the Eval spec, the same as `spec:` in YAML. Nested objects are described in the
server's JSON Schema at `GET /v1/schemas` (also used by the UI builder for validation).

| Field | Type | | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `description` | string | optional |  |
| `workflow` | string | **required** |  |
| `variants` | list of object | optional | Arms to compare; defaults to one 'default' arm at the current version. |
| `cases` | list of object | optional |  |
| `dataset` | object | optional |  |
| `from_runs` | object | optional |  |
| `graders` | list of object | **required** |  |
| `threshold` | number | optional | A case passes when its weighted score is at least this. Default: `0.8`. |
| `require_success` | bool | optional | A case whose workflow run did not succeed scores 0 and fails, whatever its graders say (their scores are still recorded). Defaults to true for cases and false for from_runs, which picks run statuses itself; set false to grade runs that are expected to fail. |
| `concurrency` | number | optional |  Default: `5`. |
| `decision_provider` | string | optional |  |
| `gate` | object | optional |  |
| `sinks` | list of object | optional |  |

